==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Manga Boogie Dragon Cat''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Very similar to [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Boogie Cat]] in terms of usage. Thanks to its cheap and expendable stats, Manga Boogie Cat can be summoned en masse to take hits in place of other, more important units. This meatshield role is quite valuable, if not for the wide selection of units able to perform this role much better due to faster speed. While Manga Boogie Cat's slow movement speed is generally a con, it does have a use in preventing Zombies from burrowing or certain slow units from unleashing dangerous attacks whereas units such as [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cat]] can sometimes slip into the range of an enemy with a powerful Omni Strike attack and weaken strong pushes or defenses.

{{Job|Classification = Meatshield}}

